WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.979
Film Courage: It almost seems like the very
nature of the question “Should I…Is there

00:00:03.979 --> 00:00:05.750
something here?”

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:10.000
is not the question to be asking because it’s
not driven internally, they’re looking for

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.500
external reward?

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.929
Jen Grisanti: Yes.

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:18.920
And that is where you have to look at What
is the Desire?

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:28.980
Is the desire the big house and the parties
and everything that you think is the glamorous

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:41.300
part of the job or is the desire that you
are sending your message to the world and

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:45.910
making an impact in a positive way.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:49.570
And I think writers have to move into that
emotionally.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:57.870
I think a lot of times they are on the outside
and they are not ready for the internal desire

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:58.960
to really kick in.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:11.180
And again, I think when life humbles you then
the internal desire awakens and it becomes

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.570
more clear.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.930
And then your writing improves.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:23.780
Like I have seen writers who have been knocked
down again and again and suddenly it’s a

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:36.530
certain point that just turns their world
and really helps them own what they’re sending

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.040
out into the world.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.980
And I think that is the greatest thing in
the world when you see that happen.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:47.520
And again, that is the life process happening
mixed with professional process.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:53.970
Film Courage: So finding meaning in the work
rather than the accolades and the perception,

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:59.130
which could eventually lead to probably a
lot of isolation and loneliness because you

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:02.550
have all of that but it doesn’t mean anything…

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.920
Jen Grisanti: And that is the key to everything.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:14.560
I mean the key to everything is when I look
at when the motivation is to leave a legacy

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:25.770
and the legacy is to empower the next generation
in a strong way through communicating your

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:33.650
ups-and-downs and your lessons that you’ve
learned in this life process.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:42.230
Then the chances of, when you’re hitting
it big and everything is there, of being fulfilling

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:44.430
are greater.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.800
So I’ve seen both happen.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:53.620
I’ve definitely seen that executive producer
who thinks…

00:02:53.620 --> 00:03:01.180
like I’m going to say many executive producers
have been married three times or I mean married

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:08.989
and divorced and that is because they’re
putting so much energy into the job and not

00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:11.460
enough into life.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:21.099
And I remember one executive producer who
I asked this specific question who had all

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:30.430
that I talked about as far as the hit show,
the new marriage.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:36.650
Life was working and I asked the question
“Are you happy?”

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:41.910
And the answer was “Happiness is such a
loaded question.”

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:51.800
And it was so clear to me that the outcome
didn’t match the expectations and so there

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.560
was more work to be done.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.650
And I think there’s a value in that.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.180
Like if you use that in your writing.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:02.270
I think that this happens a lot.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:12.350
That there are writers that hit these massive
pinnacles and find that this isn’t happiness.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:18.769
And that is why I think the internal work,
it’s such an important part of the external

00:04:18.769 --> 00:04:19.769
outcome.

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:22.879
Film Courage: I’ve heard the same in music
and sports…

00:04:22.879 --> 00:04:24.469
Jen Grisanti: Everything.

00:04:24.469 --> 00:04:25.820
Everything in life.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.820
What is your purpose?

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.419
What is your calling?

00:04:28.419 --> 00:04:34.979
Are you in alignment with your internal desire
and the external outcome?

00:04:34.979 --> 00:04:36.270
Or are you limited?

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:43.310
Film Courage: Do you think it comes down to
how much personal freedom they feel?

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.680
Whether it [rests] in their creativity?

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:49.789
Because if someone at that level has probably
lost a lot of personal freedom in terms of

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:53.210
their schedule or even being able to go out
if someone knows what they look like.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:58.759
Jen Grisanti: Well and also in the writer’s
journey you have to recognize a majority of

00:04:58.759 --> 00:05:04.629
writers are not writing on the show that they
want to be writing on, you know?

00:05:04.629 --> 00:05:10.849
A majority of writers are taking jobs they
need to take to pay the bills.

00:05:10.849 --> 00:05:12.789
And that is just the way it is.

00:05:12.789 --> 00:05:18.870
But the gift of that is that’s moving you
forward to when you can write the show that

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.050
you create and produce.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:24.990
So that is the show that you want to be writing
on, you know?

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:34.060
So I think it’s keeping the end goal in
mind and always using that to motivate your

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.060
path.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:40.279
Film Courage: I use this expression a lot
in our videos but you know, knowing what you

00:05:40.279 --> 00:05:43.119
don’t want is sometimes more than half the
battle.

00:05:43.119 --> 00:05:44.229
Jen Grisanti: Yes.

00:05:44.229 --> 00:05:45.439
And it’s information.

00:05:45.439 --> 00:05:49.819
Like that’s what I always say, getting fired,
going back to that.

00:05:49.819 --> 00:05:58.339
What that tells us is it gives us information
“Okay, I was going down a path and I thought

00:05:58.339 --> 00:06:07.400
the actions I was taking were the right actions
but something shifted or changed so now I

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:15.819
have to redefine a new path and really think
about the internal desire versus the external

00:06:15.819 --> 00:06:18.509
outcome, do they align?

00:06:18.509 --> 00:06:22.811
And am I taking the right actions to hit the
outcome I want?

00:06:22.811 --> 00:06:22.825
Question for the Viewers: Are you happy with
your writing career?

